<title>MOROCCO: Total sells stake in Morocco's.</title>
<headline>Total sells stake in Morocco's.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Total SA sold its 2.69 percent stake in Morocco's Societe Cherifienne des Petroles, valued at 32.7 million dirhams ($3.34 million) to al Watanya insurance company, a broker at Upline Securities said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said the 47,082 shares were sold at 695 dirhams each.</p>
<p>Swedish-based Saudi Corral Petroleum Holding AB bought 73.9 percent of SCP last June for 473 million dirhams ($48.27 million).</p>
<p>An official at SCP said the firm planned to undertake an investment programme worth 500 million dirhams over about 10 years to revamp existing plants, ensure environment protection and pipe maintenance, which could be approved during next board meeting.</p>
<p>SCP was last traded on Wednesday at 780 dirhams.</p>
<p>($ = 9.8 dirhams)</p>
